{{also|nott|Notts|Nott|nött|nőtt|nǫ́tt}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|nǫ́tt}}, {{m|non|nótt}}, {{m|non|nátt}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*nahts}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*nókʷts}}. Cognate with Latin {{m|la|nox}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/nouht/|lang=is}}
* {{audio|is-nótt.ogg|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ouht|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|nætur|nætur}}

# [[night]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég vakti fram á '''nótt'''.|I stayed awake until late at '''night'''.}}

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-nótt|u=u}}
The original stem is {{m|is||nátt-}} (<{{m|is||*naht-}}), preserved in the genitive plural (although the forms {{m|is||nótta}}, {{m|is||nóttanna}} now also exist) and in all stem compounds (e.g. {{m|is|nátthrafn}}). The {{m|is||-ó-}} comes from earlier {{m|is||-ǫ́-}}, created by u-mutation of {{m|is||-á-}}, a vowel change that is no longer productive.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|night}} {{l|is|njóla}} (''poetic'')

